{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the goat.</b> Rashi explained that we do not find an outer sin-offering burned except this one and the bull of the sin-offering of the inauguration, and that was by divine command; but the inner sin-offerings — we find many bulls that are burned and goats that are burned. And it is difficult from the bull of the sin-offering that we read in בהעלותך, for the Levites, where Rashi explained that that sin-offering is not eaten even though it was an outer sin-offering. And one can answer that Rashi meant that we do not find an outer sin-offering whose skin and flesh are burned outside the camp except those two; and as for how this one was not burned — neither the skin nor outside the camp — we compare it to the bull of the burnt-offering: rather all the flesh is burned near the altar, entirely, like the bull of the burnt-offering, and it is not called burning but rather offering. Some explain: it was burned because of impurity. And it is astonishing, since it was the goat of the New Moon, he should have offered it in impurity, for all communal offerings are offered in impurity, as it is written במועדו, and we derive: even in impurity. And this requires investigation."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:01.115053143Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}